<p>A passenger jet cruises above the summit. A climber on top breathes about a third of the oxygen available at sea level. The climb from South Base Camp to the summit covers nearly 3,500 meters of vertical gain.</p>
<p style="text-align: center;"><em><strong>29,031.7 feet of pure majesty. The rock, the snow, and the absolute roof of the world are waiting for you. Don&#8217;t settle for reading the maps; walk the iconic Khumbu trail with the team that handles every detail from arrival to Everest base camp. Claim Your Spot on the Trail with <a href="https://explorevisionnepal.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Explore Vision Nepal</a></strong></em></p>
